Usage: locate [OPTION]... PATTERN...

Search a database of file paths for matching names.
Run 'updatedb' first to build the database.
When a pattern contains any of *?[]\ it is matched as a
shell glob against whole paths; otherwise a substring
search is performed.  Database entries are plain path
lines (a Windows platform deviation from LOCATE02).

OPTIONS:
  -0, --null          separate output entries with NUL, not newline
  -A, --all           print all database entries
  -b, --basename      match on filename, not full path
  -c, --count         count matching entries
  -d, --database ARG  use given database
  -e, --existing      print only entries that exist on disk
  -E, --non-existing  print only entries that do not exist on disk
  -i, --ignore-case   ignore case in search
  -l, --limit NUM     limit results to at most N entries
  -L, --follow        accepted for GNU compatibility; the database stores plain
                      paths and never follows links
  -m, --mmap          accepted for GNU compatibility; ignored
  -P, --nofollow      accepted for GNU compatibility; the database stores plain
                      paths and never follows links
  -p, --print         print matches (default)
  -r, --regex         treat patterns as POSIX basic regular expressions
  -S, --statistics    print database statistics
  -s, --stdio         accepted for GNU compatibility; ignored
  -w, --wholename     match patterns against the whole path (default)
      --help          display this help and exit
  -V, --version       output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
